# Input
```ts
/* should generate diagnostics */
(x as number) * -1;
-1 * (x as number);
x! * -1;
(<number>x) * -1;
(x satisfies number) / -1;

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.ts:2:1 lint/nursery/useUnaryMinus  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! Multiplying by -1 is a roundabout way to negate a value.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ (x as number) * -1;
      │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ -1 * (x as number);
    4 │ x! * -1;
  
  i The unary minus operator is shorter and states the intent directly.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Use the unary minus operator.
  
    1 1 │   /* should generate diagnostics */
    2   │ - (x·as·number)·*·-1;
      2 │ + -(x·as·number);
    3 3 │   -1 * (x as number);
    4 4 │   x! * -1;
  

```

